anitarian aid that  many people are giving what about the  reaction of nato  do you feel it has been strong enough  well  nato is an alliance responsible firstly  to defend their own  our own members  and  currently this is happening  nato hasn't been  so much united as it is now  i don't think  in any time since the end of the cold  war  but it's not enough according to my  opinion we have to  it's it's uh it's uh proper that nato is  not directly involved in the conflict  with the with the  troops on the ground  but currently we have to do everything  to strengthen the air defense of the  ukraine  ukrainians are asking us to introduce  the non-fly zone  some of our friends are very afraid to  do this  there are reasons behind  this position  i proposed to  introduce no-fly zone  in ukraine before the conflict started  if this has happened  then  russia  would take all risk with starting the  war with the nato  in practice maybe this is not so simple  but now  there are two options  uh regarding introducing the non-fly  zone in ukraine first we have to be  aware this is ukraine this is not  russian  if this no-fly zoning is introduced in  ukraine  then this is uh on the call of sovereign  leadership of this country  and russia has no according to the  international law russia has not saying  it this is not speaking this is not  talking about introducing the nonfly  zone about russian territory this would  be  this would be threat to russia and this  would be a real uh  start of the of the conflict  theoretically in practice situation is  different  and i think that nato has to  do everything to strengthen the air  defense of the ukrainian army of the  ukrainian air forces  nato  nato actually has means to do this  it will take longer  and as you said  recently  there is also a possibility to to  introduce  limited uh non-fly zone  to  to  serve  the humanitarian purpose only i think  that  with the combination of uh these two  last approaches  we can help ukrainians a lot we can help  ukrainians a lot and with helping  ukrainians  we are helping to to defend  europe imagine if ukraine country of 40  million is taken  and we do nothing  real enough to help them  what  those who are against  helping to ukraine will say  when putin will  go further to moldova georgia  baltic states  the same people will say  oh  this is only one small country of 2  million people why to risk war  with  with  russia which is nuclear power  this is the same debate  as has happened in the 30s of the last  century and we all know what  were the consequences  so so time to be very serious time to  react is now  and i'm very glad that i see  the unity  inside of the european union and also  inside of the nato  which we have never faced during last  three decades  and this is giving hope not only to me  and to the slovenians and other nato  members especially those who are on the  border with the with the war zone now  but also to the ukrainians this is  this is the place where strength for  them is coming  janez yanska the slovenian prime  minister a pleasure to talk to you today  and thank you for explaining what people  of slovenia feel about this thank you
 

